      "knowledge_point": "Computing the Area Scale Factor of a Linear Transformation",
      "problem": "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}]?\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|6\\cdot 8-7\\cdot 4| \\\\  & =|48-28| \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
